    "novelty": {
      "score": 4,
      "rationale": "Stage attribution as a multi-class contamination task is confirmed absent from the literature across extensive search; LWSP (per-block squared gradient norms as a classification feature) and the joint contrastive objective are genuine methodological contributions not reducible to DICE, Self-Critique, or CoDeC. RADAR (arXiv:2510.08931) uses activation features for recall-vs-reasoning detection but never attempts cross-stage attribution, leaving the gap intact."
